      "problem": "What is the domain of the function $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}-2?$",
      "worked_solution": "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$",
