    "q-250599": {
      "dom_id": "step-q250599",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the range of the function $f(x)=5(x+1)^{2}+8.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\le f(x)$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex.\n\n- Since $h=-1$ and $k=8,$ the vertex is $(-1,8).$\n\n- Since $a=5>0,$ the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[8,\\infty ),$ i.e. $8\\le f(x)<\\infty .$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14244652/assets/7ff6f49b63c4ad55324bbb406558781c9f3e5af3a98d34b285c65f88746bddab.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
