    "q-250607": {
      "dom_id": "step-q250607",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-3(x+5)^{2}+7.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$f(x)\\le $\n{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "The parabola is written in vertex form, \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex. \n\n- Since $h=-5$ and $k=7,$ the vertex is $(-5,7).$\n\n- Since $a=-3<0,$ the parabola opens downwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens downwards, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $(-\\infty ,7],$ i.e. $-\\infty <f(x)\\le 7.$\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14244652/assets/252a3c0475f838b1835f2da9c3c818a938c916b781c5abaa1f12ed09c52c56f6.png)",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
